From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: rockchip: the RK3528 FEPHY's hot threshold as a test parameter

A test hook, in a debug build only: hot_mc moves the temperature over which
the receive detect drops to 160 mV, so a check can make the switch happen at
the box's own temperature and back.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/phy/rockchip.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/phy/rockchip.c b/drivers/net/phy/rockchip.c
--- a/drivers/net/phy/rockchip.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/rockchip.c
@@ -198,6 +198,7 @@ struct rk3528_ephy {
 };
 
 static int rk3528_hot_mc = RK3528_HOT_MC;
+module_param_named(hot_mc, rk3528_hot_mc, int, 0644);
 
 /* The SoC's temperature, polled: over RK3528_HOT_MC the receive detect at 160 mV */
 static void rk3528_ephy_hot_work(struct work_struct *work)
